//
// The pairs are the point. An ABSENT component is named rather than drawn, with
// a MEASURED ZERO as its control (schema.py: `host_cpu_ms` 0.0 for
// fused/coarse/runlist is a measurement -- those modes instrument host compute
// and ran none -- while an empty field means the mode reported no such
// component, and fabricating a zero for it is forbidden). A NEGATIVE remainder
// is flagged as the defect it is, with a large POSITIVE remainder as its
// control, because `device_ms.timing` states the three components are disjoint
// and "do NOT sum to avg_latency_ms" -- on the post-flip trees the remainder
// runs 37-47% for `offload` and 84-89% for `fused`, and that is uninstrumented
