// `64 * 1024`), applied in both directions per mode, and the derived `full`
// plan reproducing devq 427/431's measured counts rung for rung (7/6/5/3).
// The old "no other mode is bounded at any ladder point" clause narrows to
// 512..4096, where every mode has gated on hardware; the ends now carry
// bounds that were measured refusing. run_profile_bounds_tests.lit (3/3,
// with air) checks the same predicates against the builders themselves.
//
// `[2026-08-21]` 587 -> 611, two modules added by the branch cleanup's
// cluster B, which retired the port-loop harness: test_distinguish (+18) --
// the Phase E cross-mode distinguishability gate re-homed as
// study/distinguish.py over a profile root's recorded dispatch vectors, both
// directions per clause plus the fail-closed validation the retired gate had
// (NaN, negative, fractional counts, zero submissions, zero bytes), pinned to
// doc 54 walk 2's seq-512 vectors -- and
// test_require_turbo (+4), the refusing branches of the one live Turbo-pmode
// rule through the REAL xrt-smi parser (a stub xrt-smi on PATH, or none), as
// the retired pmode_guard selftest drove it; and test_run_profile +3, the
// profile gate refusing a walk whose modes do not distinguish, one that
// lost a declared length behind duplicate rows, and one where a skip and a
// failing length traded places (skip identity against the declared skips).
//
// `[2026-08-22]` 611 -> 617, no module added: item 8 (the iron latency gap)
// found ~22 of a 42 ms coarse forward was the per-boundary comparison running
// INSIDE the clock; run_mode gains --no-stage-stats (opt-in: the warm-up and a
// post-timed dispatch run the real comparison, the timed ones a sentinel) and
// test_run_mode pins it both ways (+6): the sentinel can never read clean, a
// failing warm-up or post-check fails the row, and the one asymmetry -- a
// mismatch confined to a timed iteration -- fails the default and not the flag.
//
